<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 126 0 R
/E (Washington and Tehran have announced the cessation of hostilities with narrow scope: toll-free Hormuz reopening, lifting the US naval blockade, mine-clearance, limited oil-export waivers. More contested files are slated for resolution within 60 days: full sanctions relief, frozen-asset release, reconstruction financing, nuclear file. But near-term challenges include: continued US naval blockade until signing of the agreement, continued Israeli escalation in Lebanon, Iranian insistence on Hormuz fees. Longer-term challenges include: lifting US sanctions and unfreezing Iranian assets is legally complex, the nuclear settlement is unresolved. For companies: hold war-risk and contingency posture through the 60-day window at minimum; tie any reactivation of Gulf-loading, insurance, or staffing decisions to verified mine-clearance and verified transit; build a plausible re-escalation scenario \(Israel-triggered breakdown; failed nuclear round\) into Q3 planning.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
